+## Local AI Office preview integration (2026-10-14)
+
+`apps/ai-office-preview` exposes DOCX layout, page rasterization, caret/selection state, an allowlisted command registry and save bytes through WebAssembly. The sibling VS Code fork supplies a compact toolbar and caret input, and its CLI uses the same bridge for editing. Formatting, tables, images, links, comments and undo/redo are covered by synthetic export/reopen tests in `../vscode/extensions/ai-office-common`. Upstream editing parity estimates are unchanged.
+
+AI Office Word editing update (2026-10-16): the preview bridge reports the current paragraph style, and insert.table accepts explicit borders so empty tables remain visible in imported documents. The host uses visual style/table menus and exports DOCX snapshots on save/backup instead of every keystroke.
+
+AI Office integration (2026-10-16): applying a built-in paragraph style to an imported DOCX now materializes only missing style definitions and their dependencies in the same undoable command. Existing custom definitions remain intact. The integration tests cover Title/Subtitle/headings, undo, save and reopen with a sparse imported style sheet.
+
+The October 17 integration adds internal identities for paragraphs, tables, rows and cells; bounded reads; atomic version-checked CRUD; targeted command results; and block rectangles for agent activity feedback. IDs are preserved by undo snapshots and the host stores validated private DOCX metadata for reopen. The host's synthetic WASM tests cover Unicode ranges, stale edits, rollback and persistence. This local bridge does not change upstream parity estimates.
+
+AI Office integration (2026-10-17): revision-checked agent batches apply up to 200 operations on a private draft and commit as one undo step. Character formatting can target validated Unicode ranges. Style inspection exposes actual resolved font sizes. Integration coverage includes paginated targets, atomic rollback with existing redo history, and save/reopen.
